# UI / UX

The HTML mockup is the **starting look**, not a lock. If Aldrin asks to add, move, or change UI not in the mockup, **do it**. Match type, color, radius, spacing. Do not invent extra chrome.

After a lasting UI change, note it in `docs/APP_CONCEPT.md` (Screens / flows).

## Mobile first

- Phone layout first (~360–430px). Unprefixed Tailwind = mobile; `sm:`/`md:`/`lg:` only for larger screens.
- Single column on mobile. Primary actions in thumb reach. No hover-only actions. Viewport: `width=device-width, initial-scale=1`. No horizontal scroll.

## Safe areas / viewport

- Prefer `min-h-dvh` over `100vh`. Pad fixed top/bottom with `env(safe-area-inset-*)` (e.g. `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]`, `pb-[max(1rem,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))]`).
- One scrollable `<main>` between header and bottom nav; reserve space for fixed chrome.
- If PWA: `viewport-fit=cover`, matching `theme-color`, safe-area on the app shell from the PWA commit (see `vue.mdc` / `new-app.mdc`).

## Building UI

- Reuse mockup visual language. Share components only after a second screen needs them.
- One clear primary action per section. Touch targets ~44px. Labels on inputs; field-level errors.
- Submit buttons: disable + loading while in flight. Destructive actions need confirm.
- Focus ring on tab; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not rely on color alone.
